From: Shadow-MSM contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: preserve resident runtime mapping across exec

The K3765-Z diagnostic transport executes from reserved physical RAM at
0x00800000. The early boot page table contains a supervisor-only identity
mapping for that runtime, but pgd_alloc() deliberately clears the entire user
half when it creates PID 1's new address space. exec_mmap() therefore removes
the mapping just before the first userspace return checkpoint can call it.

Copy the one non-LPAE PGD entry that covers 0x00800000..0x009fffff from
init_mm into every new process page table. The original section attributes
remain supervisor-only; userspace cannot access the runtime. The physical
range is already reserved by the K3765-Z device tree.

This patch is intentionally device-specific and is not suitable for a generic
ARM kernel.

diff --git a/arch/arm/mm/pgd.c b/arch/arm/mm/pgd.c
index 7f23c6d..641e56f 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mm/pgd.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mm/pgd.c
@@ -20,6 +20,10 @@
 #define __pgd_free(pgd)	free_pages((unsigned long)pgd, 2)
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SHADOW_MSM_EARLY_TRACE
+#define SHADOW_MSM_RUNTIME_VADDR	0x00800000UL
+#endif
+
 /*
  * need to get a 16k page for level 1
  */
@@ -42,6 +46,18 @@ pgd_t *pgd_alloc(struct mm_struct *mm)
 	memcpy(new_pgd + USER_PTRS_PER_PGD, init_pgd + USER_PTRS_PER_PGD,
 		       (PTRS_PER_PGD - USER_PTRS_PER_PGD) * sizeof(pgd_t));
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SHADOW_MSM_EARLY_TRACE
+	/*
+	 * Keep the initialized ARMPRG runtime callable from privileged mode
+	 * after exec_mmap() activates a process page table. This copies the
+	 * existing supervisor-only section descriptors; it does not grant
+	 * userspace access to the reserved physical RAM.
+	 */
+	memcpy(new_pgd + pgd_index(SHADOW_MSM_RUNTIME_VADDR),
+	       init_pgd + pgd_index(SHADOW_MSM_RUNTIME_VADDR),
+	       sizeof(pgd_t));
+#endif
+
 	clean_dcache_area(new_pgd, PTRS_PER_PGD * sizeof(pgd_t));
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM_LPAE
